{% source_of_truth state="current" label="Implemented boundary" %}
The current repository contains an Astro application, a Markdoc source of truth, an eight-role engineering-agent platform, and a separate in-memory business-orchestration simulation. Controlled engineering eval adapters exist; durable business-runtime infrastructure does not.
{% /source_of_truth %}

## Current repository boundary

```text
Beacon-Co
├── Astro application
│   ├── marketing site
│   ├── /docs Markdoc renderer
│   └── /workspace simulation
├── Markdoc source of truth
├── engineering agent platform
│   ├── fixed eight-role human definitions
│   ├── machine-readable contract manifest
│   ├── context/eval/tool/council/tuning policies
│   ├── credential-gated provider adapters
│   ├── agent publication and release evidence gates
│   └── redacted AgentRun/ProviderRun recording
└── orchestration module
    ├── translator + knowledge retriever
    ├── broker + provider adapters
    ├── workflows + approvals
    └── audit + documentation impact
```

## Phase 1.5 engineering control plane

```text
canonical work request
  -> approved, budgeted context
  -> provider-specific prompt compiler
  -> explainable Claude/Codex router
  -> bounded agent execution
  -> normalized tool-policy decision
  -> deterministic QA and independent review
  -> correlated run/build/release evidence
```

PR-A through PR-I are implemented repository-side and locally tested. The remaining work is evidence and external activation: a successful representative live run and repeated baseline, the required agent-platform server check, non-bypassable production approval, and real attestation/promotion/verification/rollback records. The control plane governs engineering work; it does not make the simulated broker a live business runtime.

## Broader target broker boundary

The target adds durable work units, execution management, isolated worktrees, real quality commands, fresh review sessions, provider invocation, persistent audit, and controlled pull-request preparation. No target element should be read as current merely because it appears in a diagram.

